  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Medical Laboratories (NAICS 621511) recorded $98.5M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The federal market issued 375 awards with an average award size of $263K, and obligations fell 65.7% year over year. Obligations peaked at $1.7B in FY22, then moved to $418M in FY23, $398M in FY24, $460M in FY25, and $287M in FY26 before reaching $98.5M in FY27 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs leads buying with $98.8M in obligations so far. QUEST DIAGNOSTICS INCORPORATED and LABORATORY CORPORATION OF AMERICA are the largest vendors in FY2027 to date. Current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and these figures represent contract obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed over recent fiscal years?",
